## 2. Labels — full depth

```
## 2.1 Labels kya hain exactly

Key-value pairs jo Kubernetes OBJECTS par lagaye jaate hain — sirf
metadata/identification ke liye (koi behavior change nahi karte khud
se). SELECTORS unhe use karke objects FILTER/SELECT karte hain.

Valid key format: [prefix/]name
- Prefix optional (max 253 chars, DNS subdomain format)
- Name required (max 63 chars, alphanumeric, -, _, .)
- Example: "app.kubernetes.io/version: 1.2.0" (prefix wala)
           "environment: staging" (simple)

## 2.2 Default label behavior (tumne sahi note kiya)

kubectl run day5pod1 --image=nginx
→ automatically label lagte hain: run=day5pod1
kubectl run any-name --image=nginx
→ run=any-name

## 2.3 Label commands — all variants

kubectl get pods --show-labels             # saare labels dikhao
kubectl get pods -l environment=staging    # specific label se filter
kubectl get pods -l release=alpha1.1       # 
kubectl get pods -l run!=pod5             # NOT equal filter
kubectl get pods -l 'tier in (frontend,backend)'  # multiple values
kubectl get pods -l 'tier notin (db)'     # notin filter

# Label add karo existing pod par
kubectl label pod label-demo work=tut

# Label UPDATE karo (agar pehle se exist karta hai, overwrite zaroori)
kubectl label pod label-demo work=production --overwrite

# Label REMOVE karo (key ke baad minus sign)
kubectl label pod label-demo work-

# Multiple pods par ek saath label — label selector use karke
kubectl label pod -l release=alpha1.1 work=tut

## 2.4 Spec change karne par kya hota hai (tumne note kiya — clarify karte hain)

Ye CRITICAL point hai jise most log confuse karte hain.

METADATA level change (labels, annotations, name change except certain fields):
  → Object IN-PLACE UPDATE hota hai, pod RECREATE NAHI hota
  → Existing running container affected nahi hota

SPEC level change (image, resources, ports, env vars, volumes, etc.):
  → SIRF DELETE + RECREATE se change hota hai (bare pod ke liye)
  → kubectl edit pod se spec change karo → pod ko delete + create karna
    padega manually (bare pod mein controller nahi hota jo auto-recreate kare)
  → Deployment ke andar wale pods ke liye → rolling update automatically
    hota hai (ISLIYE DEPLOYMENT USE KARTE HAIN bare pod ke jagah)

Interview answer: "Pod spec is largely immutable after creation —
fields like the container image, resource requests, and volumes cannot
be changed in-place. This is why Deployments exist: they manage the
rolling replacement of pods when spec changes rather than requiring
manual delete-and-recreate."

## 2.5 Labels vs Annotations vs Selectors — important distinction

LABELS:
  - Key-value pairs on objects
  - SELECTORS use kar sakte hain unhe query/filter karne ke liye
  - Kubernetes INTERNALLY bhi use karta hai (ReplicaSet apne pods
    dhundhta hai labels se, Service apne endpoints dhundhta hai
    labels se)
  - Short, simple values

ANNOTATIONS:
  - Key-value pairs on objects (SAME format as labels)
  - SELECTORS use NAHI kar sakte (queryable nahi, indexable nahi)
  - Arbitrary metadata ke liye — longer, non-identifying information
  - Kubernetes internally use karta hai: last-applied-configuration,
    change-cause, etc.
  - External tools bhi use karte hain: Prometheus scraping config,
    Ingress controller nginx config, etc.

SELECTORS:
  - Labels ko QUERY karne ka mechanism hai
  - Do types:
    equality-based: environment=production, tier!=frontend
    set-based: environment in (prod, staging), tier notin (db)
```

