## 3. Annotations — tumne flag kiya, full depth

```
## 3.1 Annotation add karna

kubectl annotate pod label-demo maintainer='prerit@kubcloud.tech'
kubectl annotate pod label-demo description='This is the main app pod'

# Overwrite existing annotation
kubectl annotate pod label-demo maintainer='new@email.com' --overwrite

# Remove annotation
kubectl annotate pod label-demo maintainer-

# View annotations
kubectl describe pod label-demo | grep -A5 Annotations
kubectl get pod label-demo -o jsonpath='{.metadata.annotations}'

## 3.2 Common annotations Kubernetes khud use karta hai

kubectl.kubernetes.io/last-applied-configuration  → kubectl apply ka history
kubernetes.io/change-cause                        → rollout ka reason track karna
cluster-autoscaler.kubernetes.io/safe-to-evict   → "false" means autoscaler
                                                    is pod ko evict na kare
prometheus.io/scrape: "true"                      → Prometheus ko metrics
                                                    scrape karne ka signal

## 3.3 Interview answer

Q: "Label aur Annotation mein kya fark hai?"

A: "Labels are identifying metadata that Kubernetes uses internally to
group and select objects — Services use label selectors to find their
backing pods, ReplicaSets use them to track their pods. Annotations
are non-identifying metadata for tooling and humans — they cannot be
used in selectors and are not indexed for efficient querying. Labels
should be stable identifying attributes like app name, version, or
environment; annotations should hold operational information like build
metadata, monitoring config, or the last-applied configuration."
```

