## 4. ReplicationController vs ReplicaSet — complete deep explanation

### 4.1 ReplicationController YAML — field by field

```yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ReplicationController       # v1 API — ye purana hai
metadata:
  name: nginx-rc
spec:
  replicas: 3                     # kitne pods chahiye hamesha
  selector:                       # "Mujhe aise pods dhundho"
    app: nginx                    # SIRF equality-based selector support
                                  # karta hai RC (set-based nahi)
  template:                       # "Naya pod kaise banao" (agar koi missing ho)
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: nginx                # YE LABEL SELECTOR SE MATCH KARNA CHAHIYE
                                  # (MANDATORY — warna infinite loop mein
                                  # RC kuch select nahi karega aur pod
                                  # create karta rahega)
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: nginx
        image: nginx:latest
        ports:
        - containerPort: 80
```

### 4.2 ReplicaSet YAML — field by field with all interview questions

```yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: ReplicaSet
metadata:
  name: nginx-rs
spec:
  replicas: 3
  selector:
    matchLabels:                  # Equality-based: YE LABELS wale pods select karo
      app: nginx
    matchExpressions:             # Set-based (RC mein ye nahi tha — key difference)
    - key: tier
      operator: In               # In, NotIn, Exists, DoesNotExist
      values:
      - frontend
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: nginx               # selector ke saath MATCH KARNA CHAHIYE
        tier: frontend
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: nginx
        image: nginx:latest
```

### 4.3 SELECTOR kyu hai? — interview mein specifically pucha jaata hai

```
SELECTOR ka purpose: ReplicaSet ko EXISTING pods ko IDENTIFY karna hai,
na ki sirf naye banane ke liye.

Flow:
1. RS banaya gaya, spec.replicas = 3
2. RS controller API server se puchta hai: "Mujhe wo sare pods do
   jinke labels 'app=nginx' hain"
3. Maan lo 1 pod already exist karta hai us label ke saath
4. RS controller: "1 hai, mujhe 2 chahiye → 2 aur banata hoon"
5. Total 3 ho gaye, RS satisfied

Agar SELECTOR TEMPLATE LABELS SE MATCH NAHI KARTA:
RS ban jayega, controller pods dhundhega, koi nahi milega (because
template labels alag hain), infinite pods banata rahega kyuki existing
pods kabhi "match" nahi karte. YE VALIDATION ERROR PREVENT KARNE KE
LIYE Kubernetes REQUIRE KARTA HAI ki template labels selector se match
karein.

Interview answer: "The selector is how the ReplicaSet identifies which
pods it owns and manages. It's separate from the template so that the
controller can discover pre-existing pods with matching labels and
'adopt' them rather than always creating fresh ones. This is also what
enables the heterogeneous pod scenario — a pre-existing pod with
matching labels gets adopted by the ReplicaSet."
```

### 4.4 ReplicaSet — HOW IT WORKS (mechanism)

```
RECONCILIATION LOOP (Lecture 2 wala concept yaad karo):

LOOP FOREVER:
  current = count of pods matching spec.selector
  desired = spec.replicas
  
  if current < desired:
    create (desired - current) new pods using spec.template
  elif current > desired:
    delete (current - desired) pods (deletion priority algorithm use karta hai)
  else:
    kuch nahi karo (desired state reached)
  
  sleep briefly, repeat

YE WATCH-BASED HAI, polling-based nahi:
API server se "watch" connection open hota hai — jaise hi koi matching
pod delete ya create hota hai, controller IMMEDIATELY respond karta hai
(milliseconds mein). Isliye jab tum pod delete karte ho, almost instantly
naya pod create ho jata hai.
```

### 4.5 ownerReferences — pod kis resource ke "under" hai

```
kubectl get pod <pod-name> -o yaml | grep -A5 ownerReferences

Output:
ownerReferences:
- apiVersion: apps/v1
  blockOwnerDeletion: true
  controller: true
  kind: ReplicaSet          # ← ye pod kis resource ka hai
  name: nginx-rs            # ← us resource ka naam
  uid: abc123...

Agar ownerReferences khaali hai → pod "free" hai, koi controller
manage nahi kar raha ise (bare pod).

IMPORTANT: Agar ReplicaSet DELETE karo → iske saare owned pods bhi
automatically DELETE ho jaate hain (cascading deletion). Ye
ownerReferences ki wajah se hota hai — Kubernetes knows "ye pod is
RS ke child hai."
```

### 4.6 Heterogeneous pods — tumhara scenario exactly, with mechanism

```
Scenario: 3 replicas chahiye, 2 nginx + 1 redis, selector: app=myapp

Step 1: Redis pod manually banao matching label ke saath:
kubectl run redis-pod --image=redis --labels=app=myapp

Step 2: ReplicaSet apply karo (replicas: 3, selector: app=myapp,
  template: nginx image with label app=myapp):
kubectl apply -f rs.yaml

Step 3: RS controller check karta hai: "app=myapp label se kitne pods?"
  → 1 pod already milta hai (redis wala) — ADOPT kar leta hai
  → 2 aur banata hai using template (nginx image se)
  → Total: 1 redis + 2 nginx = 3 pods, sab selector se match karte hain

Verify karo: kubectl get pod redis-pod -o yaml | grep -A5 ownerReferences
  → ownerReferences mein ReplicaSet ka naam dikhega

INTERVIEW GOTCHA: "Agar ReplicaSet delete hua to redis pod bhi delete
  ho jayega — kyuki ab wo RS ke owner ke under hai." Ye important
  side effect hai jisme log trap hote hain production mein.
```

### 4.7 Scale down deletion priority — confirmed correct, one addition

Tumhara algorithm sahi hai, official docs confirm karte hain. Ek addition jo tumne miss kiya: "if all of the above match, then selection is random."

```
OFFICIAL ORDER (memorize karo, interview mein directly pucha jaata hai):
1. Pending/Unschedulable pods pehle
2. pod-deletion-cost annotation se (lower cost pehle)
3. Jis node par zyada replicas hain us node ka pod pehle (LOAD BALANCING
   preserve karne ke liye — across-node distribution maintain hoti hai)
4. Naya pod purane se pehle (LIFO — Last In First Out)
5. Agar sab match → RANDOM

WHY DOES THIS ORDER MATTER (interview follow-up):
Rule 3 (more replicas node pe → delete pehle) ensure karta hai ki
scale down ke baad bhi pods MULTIPLE NODES par distributed rahein,
single node pe sab pods congregate na ho jayein — fault tolerance
maintain hoti hai.
```

### 4.8 RC vs RS — key difference table

```
| Feature              | ReplicationController | ReplicaSet |
|----------------------|----------------------|------------|
| API Version          | v1 (legacy)          | apps/v1 (current) |
| Selector types       | Equality only        | Equality + Set-based |
| Used directly?       | NEVER (deprecated)   | Rarely (Deployment use karo) |
| Managed by           | Nothing (standalone) | Deployment |
| matchExpressions?    | No                   | Yes |
```

