## 5. Deployments — under the hood

```
## 5.1 Why Deployment? (RS se better kyu hai)

ReplicaSet khud ONLY "N replicas running rakho" guarantee karta hai.
Agar tum image update karna chahte ho, RS tumhe MANUALLY:
  1. Old RS ka image update karna padta
  2. Old pods delete karne padte
  3. Naye pods create karne padte

Deployment ye sab AUTOMATICALLY karta hai ek defined strategy ke saath.

## 5.2 How Deployment works internally (under the hood)

Deployment → creates/manages → ReplicaSet(s) → creates/manages → Pods

Har rollout (image/spec change) par:
- Deployment ek NAYA ReplicaSet create karta hai (naye spec ke saath)
- Old RS ko SCALE DOWN karta hai (0 tak)
- New RS ko SCALE UP karta hai (desired count tak)
- Old RS DELETE NAHI HOTA — woh "revision history" ke liye KEEP hota hai
  (rollback ke liye kaam aata hai — isliye `kubectl rollout undo` possible hai)

Verify karo:
kubectl get rs                    # multiple RS dikhenge — ek current, purane wale
kubectl get rs -o wide            # SELECTOR column mein "pod-template-hash" dikhega

pod-template-hash: Deployment har naye RS ko ek unique hash assign
karta hai jo pod template ke content se generate hota hai. Isliye
same-spec rollout same RS reuse karta hai.

## 5.3 SLA aur Deployment ka connection (tumne note kiya)

SLA = Service Level Agreement = "kitna uptime guarantee hai"

99.9% uptime   = 8.7 hours downtime/year (acceptable for many)
99.99% uptime  = 52 minutes downtime/year (high availability)
99.999% uptime = 5 minutes downtime/year (five nines — very hard)

Deployment ROLLING UPDATE strategy ensure karta hai ki update ke dauraan
KUCH PODS HAMESHA RUNNING RAHEIN — isliye zero-downtime deployment possible
hai → higher SLA achieve hoti hai.

2 key parameters:
maxUnavailable: maximum kitne pods update ke dauraan unavailable ho
  sakte hain (default: 25% of desired)
maxSurge: update ke dauraan desired se EXTRA kitne pods temporarily
  run kar sakte hain (default: 25% of desired)

Example: replicas: 4, maxUnavailable: 1, maxSurge: 1
  → Update ke dauraan minimum 3 pods hamesha running
  → Maximum 5 pods temporarily (4 + 1 surge)
  → Ek-ek pod replace hota hai = rolling update
```

