```bash
## ⚠️ CORRECTION: "kubectl rollback" EXIST NAHI KARTA
## Tumhare notes mein "kubectl rollback undo" likha hai — YE WRONG HAI
## Correct command: "kubectl rollout undo"

## FULL ROLLOUT WORKFLOW (exam mein exact sequence yaad karo):

# Step 1: Deployment banao
kubectl create deployment rollout-demo --image=nginx:1.25

# Step 2: Change-cause annotate karo (history meaningful banane ke liye)
kubectl annotate deployment rollout-demo kubernetes.io/change-cause="Initial deploy nginx 1.25"

# Step 3: Image update karo
kubectl set image deployment/rollout-demo nginx=nginx:1.26

# Step 4: Cause annotate karo
kubectl annotate deployment rollout-demo kubernetes.io/change-cause="Update to nginx 1.26" --overwrite

# Step 5: Rollout status check karo (real-time progress)
kubectl rollout status deployment/rollout-demo

# Step 6: History dekho
kubectl rollout history deployment/rollout-demo
# Output:
# REVISION  CHANGE-CAUSE
# 1         Initial deploy nginx 1.25
# 2         Update to nginx 1.26

# Step 7: Specific revision ka detail dekho
kubectl rollout history deployment/rollout-demo --revision=1

# Step 8: Rollback karo (previous revision par)
kubectl rollout undo deployment/rollout-demo

# Step 9: Specific revision par rollback karo
kubectl rollout undo deployment/rollout-demo --to-revision=1

# Step 10: Rollback ke baad history dekho — IMPORTANT BEHAVIOR
kubectl rollout history deployment/rollout-demo
# Output:
# REVISION  CHANGE-CAUSE
# 2         Update to nginx 1.26
# 3         Initial deploy nginx 1.25   ← REVISION 1 AB 3 BAN GAYA!
# 
# Ye gotcha hai: rollback revision number PROMOTE karta hai, DELETE
# nahi karta. Old revision wapas AATA HAI lekin ab highest number
# ke saath. Revision 1 "gone" nahi hua — wo revision 3 ban gaya.

# Pause/Resume (tumhare notes mein nahi tha — exam mein aata hai)
kubectl rollout pause deployment/rollout-demo   # update temporarily rok do
kubectl rollout resume deployment/rollout-demo  # resume karo

# Restart (pods recreate karo bina image change kiye — ConfigMap update ke baad)
kubectl rollout restart deployment/rollout-demo

## StatefulSet — tumne flag kiya "organized manner" — brief explanation

StatefulSet ReplicaSet ka alternative hai jab pods ka ORDER aur IDENTITY
matter karta hai:

1. ORDERED STARTUP: pod-0 pehle ready hota hai, phir pod-1, phir pod-2
   (RS mein sab parallel banate hain)
2. STABLE NETWORK IDENTITY: pod names predictable hain (myapp-0, myapp-1)
   aur DNS names stable rehte hain (myapp-0.myapp.default.svc.cluster.local)
3. STABLE STORAGE: Har pod ka apna DEDICATED PVC hota hai jo pod delete/
   recreate pe bhi PRESERVE hota hai

Use case: Databases (MySQL, PostgreSQL, MongoDB) jahan har instance ka
  apna data storage chahiye aur order matter karta hai (primary/replica setup)

Interview: "ReplicaSet is for stateless workloads where any pod is
interchangeable. StatefulSet is for stateful workloads where each pod
has a unique identity, ordered deployment, and stable dedicated storage
that persists across pod restarts."

